                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_101">Cambridge,
                        Cambridgeshire. Jesus College. </orgName><p>‘Liber m. Johannis gunthorp’
                        decani Wellensis emptus London xx decembris ao xpi 1484to pro quindecim
                        solidis solutis’ (inside front cover)</p><p>CBMLC 10, 697 says that this was
                        given to Jesus by Gunthorpe, but on what evidence is not clear. Note that
                        James does not include Gunthorpe in his ‘List of donors of manuscripts’ (p .
                        117), but in his ‘List of owners of manuscripts’ (ibid.). He thus does not
                        seem to have reached the conclusion drawn by CBMLC. Leland does write of
                        another MS (no longer extant), ‘Huius codicis possessor olim fuit Gulielmus
                        \Ioannes/ Gunthorp qui in Italia cum Frea bonis studuerat literis et postea
                        factus Decanus Wellensis, multos libros in Italia manu scriptos collegio
                        Iesu dono dedit.’ (CBMLC 10, 280). He also gave to Jesus CUL MS Ff.6.20
                        (q.v.)</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">John Gunthorpe (d. 1498), dean of Wells,
                     king’s almoner, and keeper of the privy seal</provenance>
               </history>
